//RS // D-FOUND-BOARD1=A / I9: one target-profile hardware kernel shared by every
//RS // execution tier.  A target adapter supplies the generated fact slices and
//RS // chooses the register backend; this file owns width/access checks, volatile
//RS // operations, bounded interrupt delivery, and DMA ownership transitions.
//RS //
//RS // The generated register types carry width, access mode, and volatility in
//RS // their Rust type.  The target backend is the only place that performs raw
//RS // pointer operations.  Host replay uses JetRegisterReplay with the same
//RS // generated register type and the same JetHardwareFacts; it is not a second
//RS // semantic implementation.
//RS 
